document "Minecraft Enchanting"

description "A complete enchanting guide for Minecraft Bedrock Edition."

section "Enchanting Basics"

    text
        Enchanting is a system that adds special abilities and improvements to tools, weapons, armor, and some other items.

        Enchantments can increase durability, improve combat, make tools more effective, protect the player, or provide other useful effects.
    end

    subsection "What You Need"

        list
            Enchanting Table
            Experience Levels
            Lapis Lazuli
            An enchantable item
        end

        text
            An enchanting table is the primary block used to apply enchantments directly to items.

            Experience levels and lapis lazuli are consumed when using the enchanting table.
        end

    end

    subsection "Creating An Enchanting Table"

        text
            An enchanting table is crafted using diamonds, obsidian, and a book.
        end

        list
            1 Book
            2 Diamonds
            4 Obsidian
        end

        text
            Arrange the materials in the required crafting pattern at a crafting table.
        end

    end

end

section "Using The Enchanting Table"

    subsection "Opening The Table"

        text
            Place the enchanting table in the world and interact with it to open the enchanting interface.
        end

    end

    subsection "Adding An Item"

        text
            Place an enchantable item into the item slot of the enchanting table.

            The available enchantment options will appear when the required materials and experience are available.
        end

    end

    subsection "Adding Lapis Lazuli"

        text
            Place lapis lazuli into the lapis slot of the enchanting table.

            Each available enchantment option displays the amount of lapis lazuli and experience levels required.
        end

    end

    subsection "Choosing An Enchantment"

        text
            Select one of the available enchantment options to apply an enchantment to the item.

            The exact enchantment offered is influenced by the item, the enchanting setup, and the game's enchantment selection system.
        end

    end

end

section "Bookshelves"

    subsection "Why Bookshelves Matter"

        text
            Bookshelves placed around an enchanting table can increase the maximum enchantment power available from the table.
        end

    end

    subsection "Bookshelf Placement"

        text
            Bookshelves need to be positioned around the enchanting table with the required open space between the table and the shelves.

            Decorative blocks or other objects placed in the wrong locations can prevent nearby bookshelves from contributing their enchanting power.
        end

    end

    subsection "Maximum Enchanting Power"

        text
            A properly arranged setup can provide the highest level of enchantment options available from the enchanting table.

            More bookshelves do not continue increasing the enchanting power indefinitely.
        end

    end

end

section "Experience Levels"

    subsection "Using Experience"

        text
            Enchanting requires experience levels. The displayed cost is shown in the enchanting interface before you select an enchantment.
        end

    end

    subsection "Levels Are Not Stored As Items"

        text
            Experience levels represent your current experience progress. Enchanting spends levels from your current experience total.
        end

    end

    subsection "Getting Experience"

        list
            Defeating mobs
            Mining certain blocks
            Smelting items
            Breeding animals
            Fishing
            Trading
            Completing other experience-granting activities
        end

    end

end

