section "Enchantment Compatibility"

    subsection "Incompatible Enchantments"

        text
            Some enchantments cannot normally exist together on the same item.

            For example, an item generally cannot have multiple mutually exclusive protection enchantments through ordinary enchanting methods.
        end

    end

    subsection "Checking Compatibility"

        text
            When combining items or enchanted books with an anvil, incompatible enchantments may prevent certain combinations from being performed.
        end

    end

end

section "Enchanted Books"

    subsection "What Are Enchanted Books?"

        text
            Enchanted books store enchantments that can be transferred to compatible items using an anvil.
        end

    end

    subsection "Using An Enchanted Book"

        list
            Obtain an enchanted book.
            Place the item you want to enchant into the first anvil slot.
            Place the enchanted book into the second slot.
            Check the resulting item.
            Confirm the operation if you have the required experience.
        end

    end

    subsection "Sources Of Enchanted Books"

        text
            Enchanted books can be obtained through several activities, including enchanting books and obtaining them through certain forms of loot or trading.
        end

    end

end

section "Anvils"

    subsection "What Is An Anvil?"

        text
            An anvil allows you to combine compatible enchanted items, apply enchanted books, repair certain items, and rename items.
        end

    end

    subsection "Combining Enchantments"

        text
            Compatible enchanted items or enchanted books can be combined with an item through an anvil.

            Combining items can transfer compatible enchantments and may increase their enchantment levels when the applicable rules allow it.
        end

    end

    subsection "Anvil Costs"

        text
            Anvil operations can require experience levels.

            The cost depends on the operation and the items involved.
        end

        note
            Repeatedly modifying the same item can make later anvil operations increasingly expensive.
        end

    end

end

section "Repairing Enchanted Items"

    subsection "Repairing With An Anvil"

        text
            Some items can be repaired with an anvil using suitable materials or another compatible item.

            Repairing can preserve enchantments depending on the items and operation being used.
        end

    end

    subsection "Mending"

        text
            Mending is an enchantment that uses collected experience to restore durability to an item instead of adding that experience directly to the player's level total when the item is eligible to receive it.
        end

    end

    subsection "Unbreaking"

        text
            Unbreaking gives an item a chance to avoid losing durability when it is used.
        end

    end

end

section "Removing Enchantments"

    subsection "Grindstone"

        text
            A grindstone can remove applicable enchantments from items.

            Removing enchantments can return some experience, but curse enchantments are not removed by a grindstone.
        end

    end

    subsection "Curses"

        text
            Curse enchantments have special behavior and are designed to make certain items more difficult to remove or manage.
        end

        list
            Curse of Binding
            Curse of Vanishing
        end

    end

end

section "Enchanting Strategy"

    subsection "Choosing Enchantments"

        text
            Consider how you use an item before spending valuable experience and materials on enchantments.

            A mining tool, combat weapon, armor piece, and utility item can benefit from different enchantment combinations.
        end

    end

    subsection "Using Enchanted Books"

        text
            Enchanted books can give you more control over the enchantments you apply than relying only on the options offered by an enchanting table.
        end

    end

    subsection "Combining Items"

        text
            An anvil can be used to build stronger enchantment combinations by combining compatible enchanted items and books.
        end

    end

end

section "Useful Enchanting Tips"

    tip
        Build an enchanting setup with properly positioned bookshelves before spending large amounts of experience.
    end

    tip
        Keep lapis lazuli available when planning to enchant several items.
    end

    tip
        Check all available enchantment options before choosing one.
    end

    tip
        Use enchanted books when you need a specific enchantment that is difficult to obtain directly from the enchanting table.
    end

    tip
        Keep valuable enchanted equipment safe before experimenting with an anvil or grindstone.
    end

    tip
        Remember that some enchantments are mutually exclusive.
    end

end

section "Enchanting Troubleshooting"

    subsection "No Strong Enchantments"

        list
            Check the bookshelf placement.
            Make sure the required space around the enchanting table is clear.
            Check your available experience levels.
            Check that you have enough lapis lazuli.
        end

    end

    subsection "An Enchantment Cannot Be Applied"

        text
            The item may not support that enchantment, the enchantment may be incompatible with an existing enchantment, or the selected operation may not support the combination.
        end

    end

    subsection "Anvil Says The Items Cannot Be Combined"

        text
            Check whether the items are compatible and whether their enchantments can exist together.

            Some combinations are intentionally prevented by Minecraft's enchantment rules.
        end

    end

end

section "Important Notes"

    note
        This guide is for Minecraft Bedrock Edition.
    end

    note
        Enchantment availability, compatibility, costs, and mechanics can change between Minecraft versions.
    end

    note
        The exact enchantments offered by an enchanting table are generated by Minecraft's enchantment system and are not guaranteed to be the same every time.
    end

    note
        Enchantments obtained through commands or other unusual methods may follow different rules from normal survival enchanting.
    end

end

